{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c4"],"primary":"c1","title":"Los Angeles Just Cause for Eviction Ordinance (JCO)","requirement":"Landlords of JCO units may end a tenancy only for an at-fault or no-fault just cause listed in the ordinance. Before a no-fault eviction they must file a Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD and pay relocation assistance within 15 days of serving notice. All eviction notices must be filed with LAHD within 3 business days of service. Non-payment evictions are barred unless the amount owed exceeds the Fair Market Rent for the unit's bedroom size.","key_value":"No-fault relocation assistance (2026-07-01 to 2027-06-30): eligible tenants $11,000 (under 3 years) or $14,400 (3+ years or low income); qualified tenants $23,150 or $27,400. A natural-person single-family owner pays one month's rent. Non-payment eviction only if the amount owed exceeds Fair Market Rent. Eviction notices must be filed with LAHD within 3 business days.","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"L.A.M.C. § 165.03 (Just Cause for Eviction Ordinance)","coverage_conditions":"Most residential properties in the City of Los Angeles not regulated by the RSO, including buildings newer than October 1, 1978 and a property with only one single-family dwelling. Applies once the tenant has lived in the unit 6 months or the original lease has expired, whichever comes first. Qualified tenants are age 62+, handicapped or disabled, or have a minor dependent child.","exemptions":"Transient hotels; licensed care facilities; fraternity or sorority houses; the owner's roommate; cooperatives in certain circumstances; some non-profit homeless facilities or short-term substance abuse treatment centers; some HACLA- or government-owned properties; units already subject to the RSO; tenancies under 6 months where the original lease has not expired. No relocation is owed when one resident manager replaces another, or for natural-disaster hazards not caused by landlord negligence. Accumulated rent may be offset against relocation, except for government orders to vacate.","coverage_from":"c1","conflict_note":null},{"members":["c2","c3"],"primary":"c3","title":"Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance: eviction for legal reasons and no-fault relocation assistance","requirement":"Tenancies in RSO units may be ended only for legal at-fault or no-fault reasons. For a no-fault eviction the landlord must first file a Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD, give the required written notice, and pay relocation assistance within 15 days of serving notice (or place it in escrow). Termination notices must be filed with LAHD within 3 business days of service.","key_value":"No-fault relocation assistance (2026-07-01 to 2027-06-30): eligible tenants $11,000 (under 3 years) or $14,400 (3+ years or low income); qualified tenants $23,150 or $27,400; Mom and Pop properties $10,550 (eligible) or $21,250 (qualified). Amounts increase every July 1. Notice is 30 or 60 days; some evictions require 120 days or up to a 1-year extension.","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"L.A.M.C. § 151.09","coverage_conditions":"Rental units covered by the RSO, generally first built on or before October 1, 1978, plus other covered unit types. Qualified tenants are age 62+, handicapped or disabled, or have a minor dependent child. The Mom and Pop reduction requires all of the following: a building of 4 or fewer units; no use of the provision in the prior 3 years; a landlord owning no more than 4 units plus one single-family home on a separate lot in LA; and any relative not owning residential property in LA.","exemptions":"Units exempt from the RSO. No relocation is owed when one resident manager replaces another, or for natural-disaster hazards not caused by landlord negligence. Accumulated rent may be offset against relocation, except for government orders to vacate. Demolition of Protected Units for new construction is governed by the RPO and HCA instead.","coverage_from":"c2","conflict_note":null},{"members":["c5"],"primary":"c5","title":"Los Angeles Resident Protections Ordinance (RPO): demolition of Protected Units for new construction","requirement":"Owners who demolish Protected Units for new construction within 5 years after filing an Intent to Withdraw or Declaration of Intent to Evict must follow RPO relocation rules and pay the highest applicable State or City amount. Occupants have rights to relocation, to remain up to 6 months before construction (with 6 months' notice), to return if demolition does not proceed, and in some cases to first refusal.","key_value":"Option 1 payments to lower-income households (2026-07-01 to 2027-06-30): extremely low income $115,480; very low income $96,750; low income $87,450. Households above low income receive RSO/JCO amounts.","status":"in_force","effective_date":"2025-02-11","end_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Ordinance Nos. 188481 and 188482","coverage_conditions":"Only Protected Units (including all RSO units) demolished for new construction.","exemptions":null,"coverage_from":"c5","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
